---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout current="/" description="Richard J. Allen is an operations and customer-success leader with experience in people management, SaaS support, process improvement, training, reporting, and cross-functional execution.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Operations Management · Customer Success · Process Improvement · People Leadership</div>
    <h1>Helping people, processes, customers, and operations work better together.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Richard Allen, an operations and customer-success leader based in Oregon. My background combines direct people management, SaaS/software support, customer experience, process improvement, project coordination, operational reporting, training, supply operations, and change leadership. I’m strongest in work where teams need structure, performance needs to be measurable, and complex operations need to become clearer and more repeatable.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">View selected work</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Career impact at a glance</div><h2>Work that turns complexity into something usable.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from operations, reporting, SaaS support, and process-improvement work.</p></div>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">100</span></div><div class="metric-label">new SOPs created, plus 25+ legacy SOPs corrected and standardized in a year-long program</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">400+</span></div><div class="metric-label">workforce position records managed across multiple Oregon Health Authority divisions</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">20+</span></div><div class="metric-label">recurring and specialized workforce reports maintained for leadership</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">32</span></div><div class="metric-label">Customer Support and Technical Support representatives managed after promotion to Customer Support Manager</div></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>Where I add value</h2>
    <div class="grid two value-grid">
      <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">01</div><h3>Operations & people management</h3><p>Promoted to Customer Support Manager in 2015 with direct hiring, firing, discipline, performance, workflow, quality, coaching, and operational responsibility. Earlier warehouse-management experience adds supply, inventory, driver, and mixed-workforce leadership.</p><a href="/operations-leadership/">Operations & leadership →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">02</div><h3>Customer success & SaaS leadership</h3><p>Customer relationships, technical support, escalations, training, software adoption, customer-lifecycle work, retention improvement, and leadership of a 32-person Customer Support and Technical Support organization.</p><a href="/customer-success/">Customer success experience →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">03</div><h3>Process improvement & governance</h3><p>Led a year-long SOP project and team, created 100 new SOPs, corrected and standardized 25+ legacy SOPs, built the repository and governance model, coached contributors, and established ongoing creation and maintenance standards.</p><a href="/process-improvement/">Process improvement work →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">04</div><h3>Implementation & enablement</h3><p>Project-managed software migrations, prepared teams for major product changes, validated software builds, coordinated developers and support staff, and created training, procedures, and customer-facing instructional content.</p><a href="/implementation-enablement/">Implementation & enablement →</a></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section project-work-home"><div class="container">
    <div class="project-teaser">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow light">Also available for selected project work</div>
        <h2>Need an important process documented clearly?</h2>
        <p>I take on selected short-term projects involving SOP development, workflow documentation, training guides, existing-procedure cleanup, and customer-support documentation. This is a focused project-work lane alongside my primary search for the right long-term role.</p>
        <div class="service-chips"><span>SOPs</span><span>Workflow documentation</span><span>Training guides</span><span>Process cleanup</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/contact/">Discuss a project</a><a class="text-link-light" href="/process-improvement/">See documentation services →</a></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="callout"><strong>Leadership beyond the workplace.</strong> Volunteer hospital chaplaincy, youth mentoring, community administration, and disaster-response service have reinforced the same habits I value professionally: listening, organizing, mentoring, communicating clearly, and helping people through difficult situations. <a href="/community-leadership/">See community & volunteer leadership →</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
